	<h2><span class="anchor-hash">#</span>overview</h2>
	<p>
		The house runs an Advantage Air / MyAir HVAC system whose wall controller is a Samsung
		Galaxy Tab talking to the vendor's Control Box (CB) over RS-485. This project replaces the
		tablet's role as the RS-485 talker with a Raspberry Pi Zero W running a Rust daemon
		(<code>cb-daemon</code>) — a register mailbox sync engine that exposes a single-session
		WebSocket API for control and state. The tablet now acts purely as a WebSocket client, and
		the old USB path remains intact for instant rollback.
	</p>

	<h2><span class="anchor-hash">#</span>architecture</h2>
<pre><code>┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                 Advantage Air CB Hardware                    │
└──────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┘
                               │ RS-485 half-duplex (57600 8N1)
                               │ Ping ↔ setCAN ↔ getCAN ↔ ackCAN
                               ▼
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│      cb-daemon — airconcb (Raspberry Pi Zero W)              │
│  • Rust register mailbox sync engine (7-byte registers)     │
│  • Single active session enforced (WS close 4009)           │
│  • OpenRC supervise-daemon, unlimited respawn               │
│  • CH340 USB-RS485 dongle → /dev/ttyUSB0                    │
└──────────────────────────────┬───────────────────────────────┘
                               │ ws://&lt;host&gt;:2026/v1/mailbox-stream
                               ▼
┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│      aaservice2 — wall tablet (Galaxy Tab A 8.0)             │
│  • MyAir UI (myair5) serving legacy :2025 API               │
│  • Transport-neutral; watchdog-guaranteed start             │
│  • Telemetry → InfluxDB / Grafana                           │
└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘</code></pre>

	<h2><span class="anchor-hash">#</span>components</h2>

	<h3>cb-daemon <span class="badge">rust</span></h3>
	<p>
		The heart of the bridge: maintains an in-memory mirror of the CB's register bank and syncs
		it over the RS-485 bus. Exposes clean JSON schemas mapped 1:1 to hardware registers.
		Strictly one active WebSocket client at a time — a second client is rejected with WS close
		code <code>4009</code> to prevent split-brain state mutations on the bus.
	</p>

	<h3>airconcb <span class="badge">alpine linux · armv6</span></h3>
	<p>
		Raspberry Pi Zero W (Alpine 3.24, OpenRC). RS-485 tap (pins 1–2 A/B, 4/6 GND), ~14 V feed
		via 1 A T fuse → buck → PWR. Logging is RAM-backed (tmpfs, 128 MiB) with aggressive
		logrotate — volatile across reboot by design.
	</p>

	<h3>wall tablet <span class="badge">android 11 · lineageos 18.1</span></h3>
	<p>
		Samsung Galaxy Tab A 8.0 (SM-T350), Magisk-rooted, running the vendor MyAir UI. Its
		<code>aaservice2</code> app is now a pure WS client; every register read/write travels
		through the Pi. Battery held at 40–45% via <code>batt_slate_mode</code>, with battery and
		system metrics pushed to InfluxDB.
	</p>

	<h2><span class="anchor-hash">#</span>register mailboxes</h2>
	<p>The WS API maps 1:1 to the CB's 7-byte register mailboxes:</p>
	<table>
		<thead>
			<tr>
				<th>reg</th>
				<th>name</th>
				<th>role</th>
			</tr>
		</thead>
		<tbody>
			<tr>
				<td><code>01</code></td>
				<td>zone config</td>
				<td>total zones, constant zone IDs, filter clean flag</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>02</code></td>
				<td>unit activation</td>
				<td>AC brand (Daikin 0x11, Panasonic 0x12…), code activation</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>03</code></td>
				<td>zone state (JZ11)</td>
				<td>zone #, open/close bit + damper %, sensor type, set/measured temp</td>
			</tr>
			<tr>
				<td><code>04 · 05 · 08 · 12</code></td>
				<td>additional mailboxes</td>
				<td>remaining register bank, mirrored in the engine snapshot (~27 records)</td>
			</tr>
		</tbody>
	</table>

	<h2><span class="anchor-hash">#</span>safety &amp; rollback</h2>
	<div class="callout warn">
		<span class="callout-label">rule</span>
		Never run two talkers on the CB RS-485 segment. Rollback = disconnect the Pi's RS-485 tap,
		reconnect the tablet cable path — the tablet resumes driving the bus as before.
	</div>

